<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The curated mutation run: five minutes, and part of the normal loop.

  Line coverage says a line ran. It does not say a test would notice if the
  line were wrong. This run changes the source on purpose and checks that the
  suite turns red. A surviving mutant is a line no assertion observes.

    just mutants

  These six files are the ones the first sweep found gaps in, kept together so
  the run stays short enough to be worth repeating. `just mutants-all` covers
  the rest of lib/ and takes hours.

  Three survivors are the floor, and all three are equivalent mutants — the
  changed code cannot behave differently, so no test can detect them:

  - parser_utils.dart, `end <= start`: the trims move both bounds towards each
    other and stop when they meet, so end is never below start;
  - parser_utils.dart, `endIdxInSlice <= 0`: the search starts at index 1, so
    it returns a positive index or -1, never 0;
  - path_utils.dart, `identicalSync(path, other)`: the relation is symmetric.

  A fourth survivor means a real gap. Read coverage/mutation for the line.

  Commands, exclusions and the quality gate live in tool/mutation/rules.xml.
-->
<mutations version="1.2">
  <files>
    <file>lib/src/validation.dart</file>
    <file>lib/src/parser_utils.dart</file>
    <file>lib/src/lookup.dart</file>
    <file>lib/src/include_path_utils.dart</file>
    <file>lib/src/include_traversal.dart</file>
    <file>lib/src/path_utils.dart</file>
  </files>
</mutations>
